1
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:09,197
YAMU!

2
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:11,717
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

3
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:12,720
YAMU!

4
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:31,500
Your moves!

5
00:01:06,760 --> 00:01:07,920
She's our opponent?

6
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:09,500
Surely they jest!

7
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:12,180
I can defeat her with my arms in shackles!

8
00:01:12,460 --> 00:01:15,020
I'll teach these fools
to mock me! Get her!

9
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:22,739
Don't hold back your rage, my dear!

10
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:25,096
Show us the beast that dwells within!

11
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:30,900
I have never seen Master Ak-Nahdin behave
this way, Bringing harm upon the innocent?

12
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:34,160
I knew she wouldn't fight back!

13
00:01:36,480 --> 00:01:41,280
I was told this child possesses the
most powerful creature ever imagined.

14
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:44,778
So why does she not call it
forth to protect herself?

15
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:48,640
That light!

16
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:49,980
It's blinding!

17
00:01:54,340 --> 00:01:56,057
Now finish her off!

18
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:58,780
She's wasted enough of my time!

19
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,440
I must see her power!

20
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:02,160
Why does she hesitate?

21
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:04,601
Perhaps she is not who I thought.

22
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:09,440
No, I cannot allow this
madness to continue.

23
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:16,920
Show yourself!

24
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:19,600
Almighty duo!

25
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:24,420
If you want to fight, then fight me!

26
00:02:26,820 --> 00:02:27,650
Sato!

27
00:02:27,733 --> 00:02:28,700
Get back here!

28
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:32,960
Fear not.

29
00:02:33,180 --> 00:02:34,180
You are safe now.

30
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:35,500
Thank you, sir.

31
00:02:36,860 --> 00:02:37,690
All right.

32
00:02:37,773 --> 00:02:39,000
Call off your beasts.

33
00:02:40,220 --> 00:02:42,985
You have a lot of nerve
showing your face here.

34
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:46,657
You're the reason we were forced to
live in this dungeon in the first place.

35
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:48,740
Now it's time to return the favor.

36
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:53,098
Let us show this sacred guardian how
things are done below the palace.

37
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:57,257
Sento, for the last time, don't do this!

38
00:02:57,340 --> 00:02:58,240
Quiet, old man!

39
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:01,760
The pharaoh's servant wants to be a hero!

40
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:04,300
So who are we to stand in his way?

41
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:06,960
Go ahead, Sento! Save her!

42
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:09,920
You leave me with no
choice! Then let's duel!

43
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:12,240
Duos, or a sword attack!

44
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:24,910
Sato!

45
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:26,640
What have you done?

46
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:29,400
I'm slipping!

47
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:34,000
Hang on to me with all your might!

48
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:35,960
It's no use!

49
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:41,573
I'm afraid my soul has been spared
from the shadows thanks to my creature!

50
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:44,840
But you, however, won't be so lucky.

51
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:48,940
Prepare yourself, my beast,
for its feeding time.

52
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:51,190
Sektor!

53
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:57,280
Enjoy your journey to the Shadow Realm.

54
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:58,730
Huh?

55
00:04:17,180 --> 00:04:18,600
No! That's it!

56
00:04:18,740 --> 00:04:21,080
The creature I saw when I was a child!

57
00:04:27,280 --> 00:04:28,780
So it was true!

58
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:30,130
No!

59
00:04:30,213 --> 00:04:32,417
It's the white dragon with the blue eyes!

60
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:34,441
But I thought it was only a myth!

61
00:04:35,280 --> 00:04:38,940
Please, you must use
your power to protect us!

62
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:41,020
This isn't over.

63
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:42,140
Attack them!

64
00:04:43,340 --> 00:04:44,180
No!

65
00:05:01,580 --> 00:05:02,410
Incredible!

66
00:05:02,493 --> 00:05:04,020
I've never seen such power!

67
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:09,780
Is this the work of the Egyptian gods?

68
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:13,140
See that she gets some rest, sir.

69
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,200
Do you have any idea what
we now hold in our hands?

70
00:05:17,420 --> 00:05:19,997
That girl wields a beast
with enough power to

71
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:22,786
annihilate Bakura's deer
bound with one blast.

72
00:05:23,020 --> 00:05:25,297
Of course we would need
to take it from her,

73
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:28,204
which would mean sealing
her soul away in stone.

74
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:29,577
So I would say...

75
00:05:29,660 --> 00:05:30,837
Have you lost your mind?

76
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:34,100
Don't let your emotions
cloud your reason, Seto.

77
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:36,438
That girl is your key to the throne.

78
00:05:36,580 --> 00:05:41,300
We already have a pharaoh, and I
intend to find him, not replace him.

79
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:42,794
Don't waste your time.

80
00:05:43,060 --> 00:05:46,236
Rumor has it he lost his
spirit in the pit of shadows.

81
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:48,833
And Egypt cannot survive without a king.

82
00:05:49,020 --> 00:05:51,317
Do what's right for your
country and take the throne.

83
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:52,230
That is enough.

84
00:05:52,313 --> 00:05:54,880
I refuse to listen to
another word of this.

85
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:58,377
You have disgraced the name of the
pharaoh, and I won't be a part of it.

86
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:01,580
My place is beside the
throne, not upon the throne.

87
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:05,291
And when I locate the pharaoh,
that is where I shall stand.

88
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:07,540
Now, if you'll excuse me.

89
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:09,620
Seto, wait!

90
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:16,520
If you will not seize your destiny,

91
00:06:16,940 --> 00:06:20,980
then I have no choice but
to seize it for you, my son.

92
00:06:26,460 --> 00:06:30,160
Now, Millennium Stone,
I give you two offerings

93
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:32,130
First,

94
00:06:32,220 --> 00:06:37,137
the Pharaoh's Puzzle A treasure around
which the other Millennium Items revolve

95
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:41,960
This I obtained from the King of Egypt
himself Once I cast him to the shadows,

96
00:06:42,140 --> 00:06:47,420
that is And next I offer up to you a
personal favorite of mine The Millennium Ring

97
00:06:53,520 --> 00:06:58,177
it's working as soon as all seven
millennium items are returned to their

98
00:06:58,260 --> 00:07:02,937
final resting place the doorway between
this realm and the world beyond will be

99
00:07:03,020 --> 00:07:08,537
unlocked only then can zork the dark one
be released the very being who created

100
00:07:08,620 --> 00:07:13,444
the shadow realm eons ago will return to
envelop and set up the world in darkness!

101
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:24,300
What have I done to anger you?

102
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:27,680
Akura, find me the Eighth Key!

103
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:29,668
But what is the Eighth Key?

104
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:34,700
Find it!

105
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:37,360
The Eighth Key?

106
00:07:37,680 --> 00:07:39,621
What could he have meant by that?

107
00:07:39,820 --> 00:07:40,702
Yes, of course!

108
00:07:41,020 --> 00:07:42,697
When the pharaoh defeated Zork,

109
00:07:42,780 --> 00:07:46,015
he couldn't destroy the
darkness, so he locked it away!

110
00:07:46,720 --> 00:07:49,620
There's only one way to
resurrect this beast,

111
00:07:49,780 --> 00:07:52,780
and for centuries only the
pharaoh knew the answer.

112
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:56,040
And that do-gooder didn't tell us so!

113
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:58,500
And now, he's gone.

114
00:07:59,060 --> 00:08:01,157
Still, I thought I'd figured it out.

115
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:03,997
I was under the impression that
the secret to unlocking the

116
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:07,457
darkness is to return the seven
millennium items to this stone.

117
00:08:07,540 --> 00:08:09,960
But apparently there's another element.

118
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:16,000
An eighth key, the identity of which
exists only in the pharaoh's mind.

119
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:20,197
Unfortunately, his majesty
wiped his own memory clean,

120
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:22,760
so now not even he knows the answer.

121
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:24,660
Wait, that's it!

122
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:27,016
It was in front of me the whole time!

123
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:28,180
The eighth key!

124
00:08:32,660 --> 00:08:34,777
It was removed from that tablet.

125
00:08:34,860 --> 00:08:36,507
All I have to do is find it.

126
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:47,480
Come on, guys!

127
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:51,540
Whatever you do, I beg you,
do not let go of Bobasa!

128
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:55,450
Can't breath!

129
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:58,546
Have you ever thought
about a trip to the gym?

130
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:00,190
No.

131
00:09:00,273 --> 00:09:01,103
Lucci, Lucci!

132
00:09:01,186 --> 00:09:02,820
Now what? Bobasa? Huh?

133
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:04,750
Huh?

134
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:06,620
The Nile River.

135
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:07,760
So cool.

136
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,980
So refreshing. So thirsty.

137
00:09:11,040 --> 00:09:14,040
I'm starting to think we'll
never find the Pharaoh.

138
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:17,637
I have a feeling he's somewhere
along this river, Yugi.

139
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:20,477
I mean, come on, a guy
needs food and water, right?

140
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:21,390
Right.

141
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:22,910
Yes!

142
00:09:22,993 --> 00:09:25,372
And speaking of food and water, let's go!

143
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:29,660
Oh, Masha, whatever you
do, do not do a cannonball!

144
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:47,460
I know I have what it takes
to be an elite spell caster.

145
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:49,840
I just need a little more practice.

146
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:53,150
Ah-ha!

147
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,190
Excellent!

148
00:09:57,620 --> 00:09:58,450
Up high!

149
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:00,060
Down low!

150
00:10:00,300 --> 00:10:01,180
To the side!

151
00:10:01,340 --> 00:10:02,440
Now go, go, go!

152
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:04,780
Oh, yeah!

153
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:06,768
Practice does make perfect!

154
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:10,620
Let's go!

155
00:10:11,380 --> 00:10:15,120
From river, lake, sea, or
pond, fish obey my magic wand!

156
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:25,260
I guess it's back to the spell book.

157
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:30,187
How am I supposed to do this
without Master Mahat to guide me?

158
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,080
Check it out!

159
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:35,060
Hello? Ma 'am?

160
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:36,540
Can you see us?

161
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:38,960
I doubt it, guys. Me too.

162
00:10:41,780 --> 00:10:42,820
Huh? Pharaoh!

163
00:10:43,540 --> 00:10:45,305
What happened to you, my king?

164
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:48,440
You shrunk, and you're
dressed in strange clothing.

165
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:50,000
Actually, you all are.

166
00:10:50,140 --> 00:10:51,280
I love this outfit.

167
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:53,597
Guess it's safe to assume she sees us.

168
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:55,180
She must be like Bobasa.

169
00:10:58,040 --> 00:11:00,057
Bobasa's been a very busy man, my friends.

170
00:11:00,140 --> 00:11:04,020
While you were making small
talk, I was catching big fish.

171
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:08,226
You're supposed to be searching
for the pharaoh, not for lunch.

172
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:09,310
Look!

173
00:11:09,393 --> 00:11:10,700
I found a clue, see?

174
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:14,300
Hey, that looks just
like the pharaoh's cape.

175
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:15,917
Where did you get that?

176
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,597
It was floating in the
Nile next to my lunch.

177
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:21,957
Yeah, well, there wouldn't happen to have
been a person attached to it, was there?

178
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:24,417
No, but there was some
yummy fish next to it.

179
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:26,697
Will you stop thinking
with your stomach for once?

180
00:11:26,780 --> 00:11:30,251
The important thing is we found
something of the pharaoh's.

181
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,837
That means he must be around
here somewhere, right?

182
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:35,140
So let's find him!

183
00:11:35,740 --> 00:11:39,717
If you're not the pharaoh, then this
must mean that the king is missing!

184
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:40,860
We just said that!

185
00:11:41,180 --> 00:11:43,897
Sometimes it takes me a
little while to catch on!

186
00:11:43,980 --> 00:11:45,745
Will you help us look for him?

187
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:49,657
I'm assuming you and the
pharaoh are friends, aren't you?

188
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:52,120
Actually, he's my closest friend!

189
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:54,240
Yeah, me too, the poor guy!

190
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:56,991
But I know that we're gonna find him soon!

191
00:11:57,280 --> 00:11:58,339
You're his friend?

192
00:11:58,440 --> 00:11:59,270
Mm-hmm!

193
00:11:59,353 --> 00:12:01,220
As a matter of fact, we all are.

194
00:12:01,420 --> 00:12:04,457
The four of us have been pals
with the Pharaoh for years.

195
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:06,069
Then why don't I know you?

196
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:07,937
It's a pretty long story.

197
00:12:08,020 --> 00:12:10,277
You can tell me all about it on the way.

198
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:11,713
Hey, did you hear that?

199
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:12,870
Huh?

200
00:12:13,260 --> 00:12:15,084
I take it they're not friendly.

201
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:19,026
Those guys are a lot of things,
but friendly's not one of them.

202
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:22,077
So you five promise you're
friends with the Pharaoh, right?

203
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:22,990
Yep.

204
00:12:23,073 --> 00:12:24,960
That means you're my friends, too.

205
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:36,820
How'd you do that?

206
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:39,197
There'll be plenty of
time to explain later.

207
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:40,110
Let's go!

208
00:12:46,540 --> 00:12:47,370
My king!

209
00:12:47,640 --> 00:12:48,880
Are you out there?

210
00:12:49,380 --> 00:12:50,540
Master Shaddaa,

211
00:12:50,840 --> 00:12:55,157
our men have combed the entire desert,
and there's still no sign of his majesty.

212
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:57,257
I'm not sure what more we can do, sir.

213
00:12:57,340 --> 00:12:58,222
You can't stop.

214
00:12:58,780 --> 00:13:00,877
He is out there, and we shall find him.

215
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:02,040
Good news, Master.

216
00:13:02,420 --> 00:13:04,460
We have picked up Bacora's trail.

217
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:05,870
Let's go.

218
00:13:06,820 --> 00:13:07,840
It's Speria.

219
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:10,668
She must be helping
Isis locate the pharaoh.

220
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:12,240
Best of luck.

221
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:14,485
I hope you see what we cannot.

222
00:13:27,120 --> 00:13:28,697
My Millennium Puzzle.

223
00:13:28,780 --> 00:13:30,340
It's gone.

224
00:13:32,400 --> 00:13:35,140
It's in Wakura's hands now.

225
00:13:36,820 --> 00:13:37,900
Oh, Pharaoh?

226
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:41,740
How about a history
lesson about your father?

227
00:13:42,080 --> 00:13:44,957
He destroyed my village
when he fashioned the seven

228
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:49,497
millennium items in a selfish attempt
to further his own power. Of course,

229
00:13:49,580 --> 00:13:52,017
he went on to lie to
everyone about how he planned

230
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:54,777
to use the items to
restore peace and harmony.

231
00:13:54,860 --> 00:13:59,272
Of course, I knew better than to be
fooled by a ruthless dictator like him.

232
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:01,840
All your king really desired was power.

233
00:14:02,220 --> 00:14:04,044
He wanted to control the world.

234
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:06,160
Could his words be true?

235
00:14:06,940 --> 00:14:10,217
Did my father really bring
harm to innocent people

236
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:13,006
in order to create the
seven millennium items?

237
00:14:13,540 --> 00:14:17,560
Or did he rule justly and
restore peace to Egypt?

238
00:14:18,040 --> 00:14:20,280
I wish I remembered more about him.

239
00:14:26,520 --> 00:14:29,300
What a great blessing
this day has brought us.

240
00:14:29,460 --> 00:14:33,060
For unto you is born the new
prince of Egypt, my king.

241
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:36,700
And one day he shall lead us as pharaohs.

242
00:15:05,140 --> 00:15:07,580
Oh, there's no need to cry, my son.

243
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:17,360
That's right.

244
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:19,020
You can do it.

245
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:23,860
It's all right, my boy.

246
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:26,957
Remember, everyone falls once in a while.

247
00:15:27,040 --> 00:15:28,864
That is what makes us stronger.

248
00:15:33,940 --> 00:15:35,640
Must I go with you, father?

249
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:37,320
I don't like this place.

250
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:39,365
What are we doing here anyway?

251
00:15:39,620 --> 00:15:42,326
This is something you
need to witness, my son.

252
00:15:42,620 --> 00:15:43,540
Now follow me.

253
00:15:43,820 --> 00:15:45,600
Why is it so dark down here?

254
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:47,134
You needn't be afraid.

255
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:51,040
This sanctuary is protected by
the Egyptian gods themselves.

256
00:15:52,860 --> 00:15:55,837
as long as you show your
respect nothing here

257
00:15:55,920 --> 00:15:59,977
will harm you no i won't
go any further this

258
00:16:00,060 --> 00:16:04,097
is not a matter of choice father wait stay

259
00:16:04,180 --> 00:16:07,100
close and be aware of
your surroundings at all

260
00:16:13,540 --> 00:16:14,370
times

261
